WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.300
It's often hard to tell which movies will
be big hits and which ones are destined to

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:09.100
flop, but the 2019 film calendar has a number
of potential major duds in waiting.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.240
Be glad your salary doesn't depend on any
of these films making money, and get ready

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.060
for a sneak peek at the biggest box office
bombs of 2019.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.200
Serenity certainly has a lot going for it.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:25.080
It stars A-list Academy Award winners Matthew
McConaughey and Anne Hathaway, on screen together

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:26.700
for the first time since Interstellar.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.620
But even their beautiful, million-dollar mugs
are no guarantee it will make bank.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.460
Sure, McConaughey has evolved from his rom-com
and EdTV phase.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:35.380
"Who's in that?”

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:40.700
“Burton Leon Reynolds Jr.’s in that, boys."

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:43.860
But the McConaissance has still been spotty
at the box office.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:50.110
Unfortunately, Serenity will most likely continue
this trend, mostly because the movie looks…

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:51.110
well, indescribable.

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:53.520
Weird movies are fine, but they don't lead
to box office glory.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:56.800
And Serenity doesn't just look bizarre, it
looks baffling.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:00.940
The trailers defy comprehension and consequently
nobody can tell what it's about.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:04.600
Moviegoers want to have at least some idea
what they're spending their bucks on.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:07.260
Come January 25th, it probably won't be Serenity.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:11.800
On the plus side, its competition that weekend
seems pretty light, but it's also going up

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:15.560
against the second weekend of M. Night Shyamalan's
much-anticipated Glass.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:19.800
That movie is about as mainstream as it gets
and is a case study in how to market strange

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:20.460
material.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.940
So no matter how much fun in the sun Serenity
offers, its outlook doesn't look bright.

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:31.100
Terminator, Titanic, and Avatar auteur James
Cameron is producing Alita: Battle Angel,

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:35.120
a long-gestating sci-fi adventure based on
the famous post-apocalyptic manga.

00:01:35.289 --> 00:01:40.540
Meanwhile, director duties go to former indie
darling turned Spy Kids creator Robert Rodriguez,

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:43.120
who's helming the $200 million film adaptation.

00:01:43.429 --> 00:01:47.280
If you're getting a Last Airbender or Ghost
in the Shell vibe from the trailers, you're

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:47.880
not alone.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.120
Airbender made money.

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:50.640
Ghost, not so much.

00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:55.220
Alita seems more like the latter, with its
PG-13 rating likely to turn off fans of the

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:58.120
violent source material, while doing nothing
to lure in kiddos.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:01.140
"You made the biggest mistake of your life."

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.700
There's also Rodriguez, whose last film was
2014's mega-turkey Sin City: A Dame To Kill

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:07.200
For.

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:09.840
Rodriguez is notorious for stretching a dollar.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:13.600
He made his first movie, El Mariachi, for
just $7,000.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:17.040
But this movie's budget is about 28,000 times
that.

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:20.580
It's one thing for your movie to make money
because it was so cheap to produce.

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:24.660
It's a whole different ballgame to turn a
profit on a $200 million investment.

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:28.800
Chances are, you can look for this to bomb
stateside when it hits theaters on February

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:32.200
14, with producers hoping it'll perform well
overseas.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:36.680
And if not, at least James Cameron has his
four Avatar sequels to look forward to.

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:39.319
So Captive State looks tremendous.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:40.160
Clever concept.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.160
Compelling visuals.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:41.880
John Goodman.

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:42.820
Vera Farmiga.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:44.720
Any one of those is enough to earn our money.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:49.540
Even so, it may not be enough to make this
blend of horror and sci-fi action a hit, and

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:51.150
you can blame it on scheduling.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:56.350
Captive State was bumped from August 2018
back to March 29th, 2019, where it will go

00:02:56.350 --> 00:03:01.040
up directly against Tim Burton's Dumbo, the
first of many Disney live-action remakes next

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:01.540
year.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:05.460
Captive State has a great pedigree in Rise
of the Planet of the Apes' director Rupert

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:08.120
Wyatt, but high-concept sci-fi is hit or miss.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:13.010
For every District 9 or 10 Cloverfield Lane,
there's a Jupiter Ascending or City of a Thousand

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:13.500
Planets.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.260
"Federal agent on duty.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:17.040
Leave me alone."

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:22.100
Sci-fi's a risky bet even under the best conditions
but against Tim Burton and an adorable flying

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:22.680
elephant?

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:23.460
That's tough.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:27.660
Captive State may have a chance at counter-programming,
but only if it's really good.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:32.220
We've all been burned by incredible trailers
for bland movies, so hopefully Captive State

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:33.380
won't follow that trend.

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:36.020
"You and I both know those days are gone."

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:39.280
Beware of Oscar-bait movies that come out
in the spring.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:42.620
As a general rule, Oscar season usually starts
in the fall.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:47.120
With the notable exception of Best Picture
winner Crash, springtime "message movies"

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:50.200
rarely make a dent in the public consciousness,
let alone the box office.

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:52.320
Take The Best of Enemies, for example.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:56.590
Slated for an April 5th release, the film
is about a civil rights activist played by

00:03:56.590 --> 00:04:01.240
Taraji P. Henson who co-chairs a community
meeting about school desegregation with a

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:03.460
KKK leader played by Sam Rockwell.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:06.640
Surprising nobody, the experience changes
both of their lives.

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:11.800
It sounds like either a really saccharine
made-for-TV movie or a really twisted SNL

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.800
skit, but it's actually based on a true story.

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:18.340
Henson recently starred in the Oscar-nominated
blockbuster Hidden Figures, as well as the

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:20.220
award-winning hit TV show Empire.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:24.819
Rockwell, meanwhile, recently snagged an Oscar
for his supporting role in Three Billboards

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:29.060
Outside Ebbing, Missouri, and has consistently
proven himself as a versatile character actor.

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:36.560
Hopefully the star power will be enough to
give The Best of Enemies a fighting chance

00:04:36.569 --> 00:04:37.569
at the box office.

00:04:37.569 --> 00:04:41.629
But more likely, The Best of Enemies will
disappear from theaters just as fast as every

00:04:41.629 --> 00:04:43.710
other "awards contender" released in April.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:48.780
The New Mutants is about a group of teenage
mutant superheroes who aren't turtles, so

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:50.780
that's already a huge mark against it.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:55.800
Not helping matters is the confused genre-splicing
of horror and superhero action in what will

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:59.400
be the 13th film in 20th Century Fox's X-Men
franchise.

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:03.300
Take a moment to consider how much of your
life you've spent watching X-Men movies.

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:07.240
To its credit, the series hasn't been overly
cautious about about mixing genres.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:12.069
The comedy-superhero hybrid Deadpool spinoffs
have made millions at the domestic box office,

00:05:12.069 --> 00:05:15.060
and are the highest-grossing films in the
entire X-Men franchise.

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:19.180
But those films had a huge plus factor in
their favor people actually wanted to see

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:19.680
them.

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:22.860
"Join us - use your powers for good.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:23.360
heads up!

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:24.640
Be a superhero!"

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:27.380
The reception for The New Mutants was much
more muted.

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:32.120
The incredibly dark, murky and dread-filled
trailer even had some fans mockingly saying

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:36.439
it looks like a DCEU movie, which are fighting
words in the superhero genre.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:39.560
Is there really an appetite for a Hostel-esque
X-Men movie?

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:44.460
Not long ago, Will Smith could star in a dog
shampoo commercial and it would be a surefire

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:44.960
hit.

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:49.240
But a string of bad, bland, and just plain
bizarre choices has damaged the Fresh Prince's

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:52.280
bankability — and perhaps more importantly,
his credibility.

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:55.540
Which brings us to Gemini Man, which is being
helmed by Ang Lee.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:59.580
More importantly, it reunites Smith with his
Bad Boys and Enemy of the State producer,

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:00.360
Jerry Bruckheimer.

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:06.060
"Now back up, put the gun down, and get me
a pack of tropical fruit Bubblicious."

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:11.139
The story an older hitman faces off against
a young clone of himself sounds like a lazy

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:15.779
Looper ripoff, except Gemini Man was in development
for 20 years before being greenlit.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.600
Maybe there was a reason for that?

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:20.780
It certainly feels like a movie that would
have been fresh in 1997.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:24.990
Gemini Man won't light the box office on fire,
but should at least get plenty of play on

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:25.760
basic cable.

00:06:26.189 --> 00:06:28.920
Because when it comes to movies, there is
life after death.

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:30.220
It's called the TNT network.

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:37.860
Here's the latest attempt to get the Terminator
franchise back on track.

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:40.380
You're probably thinking "Wait, another one?

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:42.419
Didn't Terminator: Whatever bomb?"

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:42.920
It did.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:46.880
Terminator: Genisys was a dud in 2015… in
the U.S., anyway.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:50.280
It made enough overseas to justify another
trip to the post-apocalypse.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:53.920
Every new Terminator movie
is basically another attempt to resurrect

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:55.120
an aimless franchise.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:59.020
Honestly, the most interesting thing this
series could do is send the T-800 back in

00:06:59.030 --> 00:07:01.169
time to stop these movies from being made.

00:07:01.169 --> 00:07:03.449
And that's exactly what it sounds like is
going happen.

00:07:03.449 --> 00:07:08.650
T6 is supposed to be a direct sequel to T2,
with Rise of the Machines, Salvation, Genisys

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:10.940
and The Sarah Connor Chronicles wiped from
history.

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:13.360
You can do that with a time-travel movie,
right?

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:17.900
Linda Hamilton is even returning as Sarah
Connor, and James Cameron is producing and

00:07:17.919 --> 00:07:19.520
contributing to the story.

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:22.740
That's good enough for a little interest,
and hopefully it will be enough to save this

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:24.580
film from bombing harder than Judgement Day.

00:07:32.770 --> 00:07:36.200
Big-screen musical adaptations are pretty
hit-or-miss at the box office.

00:07:36.219 --> 00:07:40.749
Sure, Chicago did pretty well financially,
but you can't say the same for Rock of Ages

00:07:40.749 --> 00:07:41.240
or Rent.

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:45.699
And while Andrew Lloyd Webber is one of the
most bankable names on Broadway and the West

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:47.900
End, his film record isn't nearly as impressive.

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:50.660
Could Cats end that string of box office blandness?

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:55.660
It's based on one of his most popular musicals,
and features perhaps his most famous song,

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:56.160
"Memory."

00:07:56.320 --> 00:08:00.780
However, his most popular musical, and Broadway's
longest-running show, was the Phantom of the

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:04.760
Opera, which only scared up $51 million and
change in U.S. theaters.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:09.779
There's also the fact it's coming out on December
20th, 2019, the same day as a quiet little

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:13.060
indie drama currently known as Star Wars:
Episode IX.

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:16.839
With that kind of box office competition,
chances are slim that crowds will show up

00:08:16.839 --> 00:08:18.459
to watch a bunch of dancing cats.

